\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we formulate sandbox semantics}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{environment}

\p{We formulate a sandbox as an environment restriction because tool-using
training papers vary in their executors, reset rules, and evidence. ReAct
\citet{Section 2}{yao2023react} supplies the action--observation pattern.
Software-agent systems surveyed in
\citet{Section 2.3.2}{wang2024agents} add repositories, compilers, tests, and
other digital tools. No single cited source fixes the complete object above.}

\p{This formulation makes portability a mathematical question: two protocols
that share prompts but change reset or permission semantics need not induce the
same trajectory law.}
